  data: {
    LLM: "Ensure your hands are legal (back ≥ middle ≥ front). Put your strongest hand in back, weakest in front. Don't risk fouling by making front too strong.\n\nBalance hand strength across all three positions. Consider that front hand only needs to beat other front hands - don't over-commit strong cards there. Look for opportunities to make three of a kind in front for bonus. Manage risk of fouling versus potential rewards.\n\nSophisticated hand arrangement considering probabilities of opponents' holdings. Optimal distribution of pairs and high cards. Recognizing when to play for sweep (winning all three hands). Understanding expected value of different arrangements. In Open Face, tracking exposed cards and adjusting strategy.",
